---
// =============================================================================
// DRAFT PREPARED BY AN AI ASSISTANT — NOT LEGAL ADVICE.
// This withdrawal / refund policy must be reviewed and approved by a qualified
// Finnish lawyer before MoiKit relies on it. Drafted against the Finnish
// Consumer Protection Act (kuluttajansuojalaki 38/1978) chapter 6 and the EU
// Consumer Rights Directive 2011/83/EU as amended by Directive (EU) 2023/2673.
//
// KNOWN COMPLIANCE GAP, flagged in the page itself: since 19 June 2026, Art. 11a
// CRD requires online traders to provide a withdrawal FUNCTION (a button) on the
// same interface where the contract is concluded, available for the whole
// withdrawal period, plus a confirmation of receipt on a durable medium. MoiKit
// does not have one. This page documents the email route as an interim measure
// — it does not make the site compliant.
// =============================================================================
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { LEGAL_LINKS } from "../../lib/legal";
import { SHIPPING_EUR, eur } from "../../data/kits";
---

<Legal
  title="Right of Withdrawal"
  eyebrow="Returns · Peruuttamisoikeus"
  heading="Changed your mind? You have 14 days."
  intro="Because you bought online without seeing the goods first, Finnish and EU law give you 14 days from delivery to withdraw from the purchase without giving any reason. Here is exactly how to do it and what you get back."
>
  <section>
    <span class="num">01 — The right</span>
    <h2>14 days, no reason needed</h2>
    <p>
      You may withdraw from your MoiKit order within <strong>14 days</strong>, without giving any
      reason and without penalty. The 14 days run from the day <strong>you (or someone you nominate)
      physically receive the goods</strong>. Because a MoiKit order arrives in one delivery, that is
      simply the delivery day; if for any reason your order arrives in parts, the clock starts on the
      day the last part arrives.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you cancel before we have delivered anything, just email us — there is nothing to return and
      we refund your deposit in full.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we ever failed to tell you about this right, the period is extended by up to
      <strong>12 months</strong>, ending 14 days after we do tell you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <span class="num">02 — How to withdraw</span>
    <h2>Tell us clearly, in writing, within the 14 days</h2>
    <p>
      Send us an unambiguous statement that you are withdrawing. Any clear wording works — you do not
      have to use a particular form. What matters is that it is <strong>a statement</strong>:
      returning the goods without telling us, or refusing the delivery, is not enough on its own.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>By email — the route we recommend:</strong>
        <a href="mailto:moi@moikit.fi?subject=Withdrawal%20from%20order">moi@moikit.fi</a>. Put your
        order reference in the subject line and keep a copy of the sent message; that copy is your
        proof of having given notice in time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>By post:</strong> MoiKit Oy, <span class="todo">TODO: postal address</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        You can also message <a href="https://instagram.com/moi.kit_fi">@moi.kit_fi</a> on Instagram,
        but email is safer — a platform message is harder for both of us to evidence later.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Sending the notice on the 14th day is enough.</strong> It does not matter when we read
      it. We will confirm receipt of your withdrawal notice to you in writing, without delay.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="todo">TODO — COMPLIANCE GAP: since 19 June 2026, Article 11a of the EU Consumer Rights Directive requires a withdrawal button/function on the same online interface where the order was placed, available throughout the withdrawal period, with an on-screen acknowledgement and a confirmation on a durable medium. MoiKit does not have one. This must be built before the site can be considered compliant.</span>
    </p>

    <h3>Model withdrawal form</h3>
    <p>
      You are free to use the statutory model form. Copy it, fill it in, and send it to the address
      above:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>To: MoiKit Oy, <span class="todo">TODO: postal address</span>, moi@moikit.fi</li>
      <li>
        I/we (*) hereby give notice that I/we (*) withdraw from my/our (*) contract of sale of the
        following goods (*):
      </li>
      <li>Ordered on (*) / received on (*):</li>
      <li>Order reference:</li>
      <li>Name of consumer(s):</li>
      <li>Address of consumer(s):</li>
      <li>Signature of consumer(s) (only if this form is notified on paper):</li>
      <li>Date:</li>
      <li>(*) Delete as appropriate.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <span class="num">03 — Returning the goods</span>
    <h2>Sending the kit back</h2>
    <p>
      Return the goods to us <strong>without undue delay and within 14 days</strong> of sending your
      withdrawal notice. Sending them within that window is enough.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Who pays.</strong> You bear the direct cost of returning the goods. Because a kit is
        bulky and cannot normally be sent as ordinary post, we will collect it from your address in
        Lappeenranta instead if you prefer, for an estimated
        <span class="todo">TODO: state the collection fee in euros — legally required for goods that cannot be returned by post</span>.
        Nothing stops you returning it yourself at your own cost.
        <span class="todo">TODO: if MoiKit would rather bear the return cost, say so here — that is allowed and simpler</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Condition.</strong> You may unpack and inspect the items as you would in a shop. If
        you have handled them beyond what is necessary to establish their nature, characteristics and
        functioning, we may deduct the resulting drop in value from your refund. We will explain any
        deduction, in figures, before we make it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Partial withdrawal.</strong> You can withdraw from part of the order and keep the
        rest. The delivery fee is refunded in full only where you return everything.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <span class="num">04 — Your money back</span>
    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      We refund you <strong>within 14 days of receiving your withdrawal notice</strong>. We may hold
      the refund until we have received the goods back, or until you show us proof of return —
      whichever happens first.
    </p>
    <dl class="rows">
      <div>
        <dt>The card deposit</dt>
        <dd>
          Refunded through Stripe <strong>to the same card you paid with</strong>. You do not need to
          give us any card details. Depending on your bank, the money typically appears within a few
          business days of us issuing the refund. Refunds cost you nothing.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>The cash balance</dt>
        <dd>
          If you already paid the cash half on delivery, that part is returned by
          <strong>bank transfer</strong> — we will ask you for an IBAN in your own name, because
          there is no way to reverse a cash payment. We use it for that refund and nothing else.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>The {eur(SHIPPING_EUR)} delivery fee</dt>
        <dd>
          Refunded too, when you withdraw from the whole order — the law requires us to return the
          standard delivery cost you paid, not only the price of the goods. The separate cost of
          sending the goods <em>back</em> to us is the one you bear (see section 03).
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section>
    <span class="num">05 — Limits</span>
    <h2>When the right does not apply</h2>
    <p>
      Finnish law lists a small number of cases where there is no right of withdrawal. The ones that
      could realistically touch a MoiKit order are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Sealed goods that are not suitable for return for health-protection or hygiene
        reasons, once they have been unsealed after delivery.</strong> In a kit this can cover items
        such as pillows, duvets, mattress protectors and personal hygiene products. Unopened and
        still sealed, they can always be returned.
        <span class="todo">TODO: have a lawyer confirm exactly which catalogue items this covers, and label them in the kit builder so buyers know before they order</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Goods made to your specification or clearly personalised.</strong> We do not
        currently sell any, so in practice this does not apply.
      </li>
      <li>
        Goods that deteriorate or expire rapidly. Again, not something a MoiKit kit contains today.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Everything else in the catalogue is returnable. If we ever start selling something outside the
      right of withdrawal, we will say so on the product before you order it — that is a legal
      requirement, and without it the right applies regardless.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <span class="num">06 — Not the same thing</span>
    <h2>Withdrawal versus a faulty item</h2>
    <p>
      Withdrawal is your no-questions-asked right in the first 14 days. It is entirely separate from
      your rights when something is <strong>defective</strong>, which last far longer and are set out
      in the <a href={LEGAL_LINKS.terms}>Terms of Sale</a>. If an item arrives broken, do not worry
      about the 14-day clock — write to us and we will repair, replace or refund it.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we cannot agree, Consumer Advisory Services (Kuluttajaneuvonta,
      <a href="https://www.kkv.fi/en/consumer-advice/">kkv.fi</a>) and the Consumer Disputes Board
      (Kuluttajariitalautakunta, <a href="https://www.kuluttajariita.fi/en/index.html">kuluttajariita.fi</a>)
      will help you free of charge.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
